{"type":"thinking","text":"Need make stronger cast shadows. Could add a new group of shadows before counter objects but after counter. We could add after object group? Shadows need under objects, but adding translucent shadows over objects would be wrong. Existing object groups can be edited to add ellipses. Maybe easiest add a sunlit/shadow gradient across counter at end with a dark soft band from right side, which doesn't need per object. But contact shadows matter.\n\nCould instead add a global overlay in postprocess. Shadows can be drawn manually with a blur group before objects. Add one group before counter-things with long shadows of main items: e.g. shadow ellipses. But without proper occlusion, they'd fall over counter. Fine.\n\nLet's add:\n```\n<g id=cast-shadows opacity=.22 filter=blur8 fill=#533323>\n <ellipse cx=850 cy=718 rx=130 ry=12 ...>\n ...\n</g>\n```\nBut if drawn before objects, fine. Bowls etc cover. Need not match exactly. Add around 8. This will deepen.\n\nAlso add window light patches on counter with brighter shapes.\n\nNeed elevate sky: add more gradient, cloud, sun rays, warmer; maybe add textured haze. Current sky flat but okay. Add sun's light path in the sky and golden rim on hills. Add birds. Maybe add a tree branch? Garden scene. Not necessary.\n\nNeed change colors to deeper. We can add a global color overlay:\n- `rect fill=url(#coolShade)` with linear gradient from transparent at 45% to #4b3a4b .18 at 100%, blend multiply. This gives cool shadow right side. Use new gradient defined near vignette. It will unify.\n\n- `rect` fill `#ff9d4d` screen radial left? Maybe too much. use very low.\n\nLet's first fix sink and add some detail. Then render and assess.\n\nEdit sink group."}
