ger, which is very recognizable. Since there is a moka pot and mug, a French press adds narrative. Draw:\n  - glass beaker x=1166..1228, y=650..710, coffee.\n  - black lid x=1160..1234 y=640..654, with plunger rod up to 610 and knob.\n  - handle black loop.\n  - coffee grounds at bottom.\nThis becomes a French press, clearly morning coffee. Better than ambiguous. Let's do.\n- French press base glass with coffee and grounds; lid black; plunger.\n- Carafe height to 710.\n- Add steam.\n\nBread: add crumbs and a small bowl of butter? Could add a pat of butter on board front right, but knife. Maybe add 3 crumbs. Also make loaf more golden. Add steam? no.\nBowl of lemons: add leaf and stronger shadows. Maybe fine.\n\nAdd a soft-boiled egg cup? Maybe cozy breakfast objects: a small egg cup at 930? But positions. The scene currently has enough.\n\nAdd a jar of jam? On the right counter at 1430? There is stack bowls and crock. Maybe put small jam jar between vase and bowls? Space 1345-1360 only. no.\n\nAdd hanging dried herbs between window and shelf? no.\n\nLet's edit moka and mug/carafe."}
