Add slight chromatic? no.\n- Sharpen.\n\nHowever per-pixel operations in PIL are possible with `ImageMath` or `ImageEnhance` and `Image.blend`. We don't have numpy, but can use PIL's ImageFilter, ImageChops, ImageEnhance, ImageOps. For color curves, Image.point with per-channel LUTs.\n- Compute `out = Image.merge('RGB', (r.point(lutR), g.point(lutG), b.point(lutB)))`.\n- LUTs via gamma and contrast.\n- Saturation via ImageEnhance.Color.\n- Brightness/contrast via ImageEnhance.\n- Bloom via `ImageChops.screen(img, blurred_bright)`? Screen formula in PIL `ImageChops.screen` outputs 255 - (255-a)(255-b)/255, good. To isolate highlights, create image from grayscale threshold mask tinted warm. Or use `ImageChops.multiply(blurred, mask)`. Simpler: use `ImageFilter.GaussianBlur` on whole image then blend with soft light at low opacity. \n- `ImageChops.soft_light` available? PIL ImageChops has soft_light in newer versions. Check. Could use `Image.blend`.\n- Add light leak with radial gradient generated by PIL.\n\nNeed make sure it doesn't look overprocessed.\n\nLet's create a script and test 3 variants. Use small preview 2000 maybe. Could inspect. Let's do variant with warm grade + bloom + grain + slight diffusion. Also add blur to shadows? no.\n\nLet's use PIL ImageOps and LUTs.\n\nWarm grade:\n- Saturation 1.08\n- Contrast 1.06\n- Brightness 1.0\n- RGB LUT:\n  - shadows blue -2%, red +1%; highlights red +2%, blue -3%.\n  - Gamma: R 0.97, G 0.985, B 1.03 (in gamma space, point LUT).\n- Then overlay warm radial screen from upper-left at opacity 0.1 with color #ffb55f.\n- Bloom: highlights via `img.filter(GaussianBlur(22))` and screen at 0.18. This will bloom everything, but mostly bright areas. Better mask with luminance threshold. Can create grayscale L, point(lambda x: max(0,(x-180))*...), apply as mask on blurred image and screen. Implementation:\n  ```\n  blur=img.filter(GaussianBlur(30))\n  lum=img.convert('L')\n  mask=lum.point(lambda p: max(0,p-180)*3)  # up to 225\n  bloom=Image.composite(blur, black, mask)? Image.composite(blur, black, mask)\n  out=ImageChops.screen(out, bloom) # screen full, but bloom has black where mask absent\n  ```\n  `Image.composite(blur, black, mask)` uses mask to choose blur/black. Then screen at 0.5? With mask low, okay.\n- Bloom around window and sun ~strong.\n- Paper texture:\n  - `noise = Image.effect_noise((w,h), 24).convert('L')` then blur 1, colorize? Use `ImageChops.overlay`/soft_light with gray noise at low opacity. We can blend `out` with noise overlay using `Image.blend(out, ImageChops.soft_light(out, noise_rgb), 0.15)`. Check `ImageChops.soft_light`.\n  - Canvas fibers: generate horizontal/vertical lines? Could add subtle; not necessary.\n- Vignette stronger:\n  - radial gradient mask; multiply about 0.85 edges.\n- Grain 2% via effect_noise.\n- Slight local contrast (unsharp mask).\n\nLet's test."}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_RcH8ndMoDL07vtivuuOf2323","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/vellery-k709ll60/work && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageEnhance, ImageFilter, ImageChops, ImageOps\nimport math, random\n\nsrc = Image.open('cozy-kitchen.png').convert('RGB')\nW,H = src.size\n\n# --- gentle color grading ---\nimg = ImageEnhance.Color(src).enhance(1.10)\nimg = ImageEnhance.Contrast(img).enhance(1.05)\n\ndef make_lut(gamma, lift=0, gain=1.0):\n    lut=[]\n    for i in range(256):\n        x=i/255.0\n        x=(x**gamma)\n        x=x*gain + lift/255.0\n        lut.append(max(0,min(255,round(x*255))))\n    return lut\nr,g,b=img.split()\nr=r.point(make_lut(0.96, 2, 1.02))\ng=g.point(make_lut(0.985, 1, 1.0))\nb=b.point(make_lut(1.035, 0, 0.98))\nimg=Image.merge('RGB',(r,g,b))\n\n# --- bloom on highlights ---\nlum=img.convert('L')\nmask=lum.point(lambda p: max(0, min(255, int((p-185)*3.2))))\nblur=img.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(32))\nblack=Image.new('RGB',(W,H),(0,0,0))\nbloom=Image.composite(blur,black,mask)\nimg=ImageChops.screen(img, Image.eval(bloom, lambda x: int(x*0.42)))\n\n# --- warm light leak top-left ---\nleak=Image.new('L',(W,H),0)\n# radial gradient via radial mask\nmask2=Image.new('L',(W,H),0)\nimport PIL.ImageDraw as ImageDraw\nd=ImageDraw.Draw(mask2)\n# approximate with concentric circles\nfor i in range(1800,0,-8):\n    # centered at (550,300) in 3200x2200\n    alpha=int(70*(1-i/1800)**2.6)\n    d.ellipse((550-i,300-i,550+i,300+i), fill=alpha)\nwarm=Image.new('RGB',(W,H),(255,178,92))\nleakim=Image.composite(warm,black,mask2)\nimg=ImageChops.screen(img, Image.eval(leakim, lambda x:int(x*0.5)))\n\n# --- subtle paper/canvas texture ---\nnoise=Image.effect_noise((W,H), 26).convert('L')\nnoise=noise.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(1.1))\nnoise_rgb=Image.merge('RGB',(noise,noise,noise))\ntry:\n    soft=ImageChops.soft_light(img, noise_rgb)\n    img=Image.blend(img,soft,0.18)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print('soft light failed',e)\n\n# --- vignette ---\nvig=Image.new('L',(W,H),0)\ndv=ImageDraw.Draw(vig)\nmaxr=math.hypot(W,H)*0.62\nfor i in range(0,int(maxr),10):\n    a=int(90*max(0,(i/maxr-0.45)/0.55)**2)\n    dv.ellipse((W/2-i*1.15,H/2-i*0.92,W/2+i*1.15,H/2+i*0.92), outline=None, fill=None)\n# easier: use radial gradient via resized small image\nsmall=(320,220)\ngrad=Image.new('L',small,0)\npix=grad.load()\nfor y in range(220):\n    for x in range(320):\n        dx=(x-160)/160; dy=(y-110)/110\n        r=math.sqrt(dx*dx+dy*dy)\n        v=max(0,min(1,(r-0.55)/0.65))\n        pix[x,y]=int(110*v*v)\ngrad=grad.resize((W,H),Image.LANCZOS)\nshade=Image.new('RGB',(W,H),(38,24,20))\nvigim=Image.composite(shade,black,grad)\nimg=ImageChops.multiply(img, Image.eval(vigim, lambda x:int(255-(255-x)*0.75)))\n\n# --- final grain + sharpen ---\ngrain=Image.effect_noise((W,H), 12).convert('L')\ngrain_rgb=Image.merge('RGB',(grain,grain,grain))\nimg=Image.blend(img, ImageChops.overlay(img, grain_rgb), 0.06)\nimg=img.filter(ImageFilter.UnsharpMask(radius=2.2, percent=55, threshold=2))\n\nimg.save('cozy-kitchen-graded.png')\nimg.resize((2000,1375),Image.LANCZOS).save('cozy-kitchen-graded-preview.png')\nprint('done')\nPY","description":"Test warm color grade and texture"}}
