f boots? no.\n\nMaybe draw slippers side view, not top-down:\n- Each is an elongated low mound with pointed toe and open heel, showing a dark opening at the top right, but no inner oval at top. Use shape: toe at left, top line arcs, heel at right with a vertical back. Add one smallhighlight. Current donut appearance comes from the inner oval being fully visible top-down. Instead make the inner opening a crescent/dark area only at the heel, partially occluded by upper. We can adjust orientation: draw slipper from side with heel opening not visible, just a band across. Add a fluffy trim line. That should read as slippers.\n- The left slipper can be rotated with toe pointing left/down; right slipper toe right. Pair arranged naturally. Use 3/4 top but with opening not oval.\nSimpler: shape like a clog: toe closed rounded, heel open, seen from side. Draw a thick sole and an upper covering the front 2/3, with a dark gap at the heel, and a fuzzy trim stripe.\nCoordinates similar, but the inner dark footbed should be a narrow crescent at the heel (right), not a full ellipse. Make toe cap large with decorative stitch. And add an ankle strap? Mules.\n\nLet's redo slippers after we sort light. But maybe remove and add a pair of slippers as simple soft shapes with clear toe and heel:\n```\nleft: sole (x=382..468), upper path like a shoe: M385 1052 C385 1038 396 1029 417 1029 C440 1029 451 1040 456 1052 C460 1064 451 1072 434 1073 C412 1074 391 1068 385 1058 Z fill cream. Heel opening: path from 444 1035 to 450 1050 to 450 1065 to 443 1068 etc, dark. Add band.\n```\nCurrent oval opening covers 414-450, causing bowl. Make opening narrow at heel (x=440-457) and only y=1037-1063. The toe region should be solid with embroidery or seam. Also add a slipper cuff around the opening. Hmm.\n\nWe'll fix.\n\nCabinet light: remove big diagonals, use subtle ellipses:\n```\n<g clip-path cabinet>\n<ellipse cx=380 cy=820 rx=380 ry=120 fill=#ffe6ae opacity=.2 filter=blur26 style=screen>\n<ellipse