ow casts light to the right. Our sunbeams travel right/down. Good.\n\nPost grade warm tone gives a golden morning. Nice.\n\nNeed perhaps sign the image? no.\n\nLet's make final high-res and maybe a smaller web version. Provide both:\n- `cozy-kitchen-morning.png` 3200x2200 (full)\n- maybe `cozy-kitchen-morning.jpg`? PNG fine.\n- The source HTML.\n\nBut we need decide if final image should be 3200x2200 or 2400x1650. 3200x2200 is crisp and only 6MB; finalized grade ~? 8MB maybe. Fine.\n\nCould also create a 16:9 crop? The prompt says draw; no specific ratio. 1.45 is uncommon but okay. Maybe 3:2 is nicer for wallpapers. Our composition fills 1.45. If we crop to 16:9 (3200x1800) we lose bottom floor and part of top? Could shift. Not worth.\n\nThe image currently has big top margin? no, window top at 58. Fine.\n\nLet's inspect the cat after adding details (preview crop). Render."}
